{"event":"agent","text":"**Short answer:** `rpt_board_metrics` has no direct link to `dim_accounts`. Its MRR is built account by account, but through `fct_mrr`, not `dim_accounts`.\n\n**What the tools show**\n- `rpt_board_metrics`: its grain is unknown. It has no tested or declared key, and `month_start` is probably the grain but that is a guess, so please confirm it (`ods_describe_entity`). It lists no references and no referenced-by entries.\n- `dim_accounts`: one row per `account_id` [tested] (`ods_describe_entity`). The only relationship it lists is `fct_invoices` → `dim_accounts` (many-to-one, tested). `rpt_board_metrics` does not appear in that list.\n- `rpt_board_metrics` reads only from `fct_mrr`. `dim_accounts` is not upstream of it (`ods_lineage`).\n- `fct_mrr` carries `account_id`, `month_start`, `mrr_usd`, `previous_mrr_usd`, `mrr_change_usd` and `change_category`. Its grain is probably one row per account per month, but I did not describe it, so that is unconfirmed.\n- Column lineage from `fct_mrr` into the report (`ods_lineage`):\n  - `mrr_usd` is the aggregation of `fct_mrr.mrr_usd`.\n  - `arr_usd` is also an aggregation of `fct_mrr.mrr_usd`.\n  - `net_new_mrr_usd` is the aggregation of `fct_mrr.mrr_change_usd`.\n  - `paying_accounts` is an aggregation of `fct_mrr.account_id`, with a conditional on `mrr_usd`.\n  - `month_start` is the group-by key.\n\nSo the board MRR is a per-month sum of per-account MRR rows from `fct_mrr`. `dim_accounts` contributes nothing to it. Internal and deleted accounts would only be excluded if `fct_mrr` filters them, and nothing here shows that.\n\n**Uncertain**\n- `fct_mrr` is built from `int_subscription_months`, which is opaque. ODS could not parse it (`range` table function). Lineage and filters upstream of `fct_mrr` are therefore unknown, not confirmed absent. I can't say whether trials or internal accounts are excluded.\n- Can you confirm the intended grain of `rpt_board_metrics` (one row per `month_start`?) and whether the board figure should exclude `is_internal` or `is_deleted` accounts? If so, it would need a join from `fct_mrr` to `dim_accounts`, and I can describe `fct_mrr` and plan that join."}
{"event":"human","text":"Is that the same as saying one is built from the other in dbt?"}
{"event":"agent","text":"No. Two models can be related without either being built from the other.\n\n- **Built from (dbt lineage):** one model selects from another through `ref()`. This is a dependency in the DAG. `rpt_board_metrics` is built from `fct_mrr` this way. `dim_accounts` is not upstream of it, according to `ods_lineage`.\n- **Related (keys):** two tables share a key that you can join on, usually shown by a `relationships` test. `fct_invoices` → `dim_accounts` is an example, and the test is tested and many-to-one. Neither table is built from the other. They just join on `account_id`.\n\nFor your question, `fct_mrr` has an `account_id` column, so it can probably be joined to `dim_accounts`. But `ods_describe_entity` shows no relationship between them, tested or declared. I haven't described `fct_mrr`, so I can't tell you whether one exists there. And `rpt_board_metrics` has no `account_id` column at all, since it is aggregated by month. It can't be joined to `dim_accounts` directly, so the only possible path is through `fct_mrr`.\n\nI can describe `fct_mrr` and run `ods_erd` on it if you want to check whether the join to `dim_accounts` is tested."}
